        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Foiled White House attack: Group planned to use snipers and drones, says FBI Issued on: 17/06/2026 - 14:19 The FBI has said it thwarted a planned attack on the UFC mixed martial arts event on the White House lawn on the weekend, with the attackers allegedly planning to use explosive-laden drones to strike the north side of the White House while snipers would shoot people as they fled. Five people have been charged over the plot and they were allegedly motivated in part by anger at the handling of investigative files related to sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. Makerfield: the local election that could change the UK 17/06/2026 Europe Brazil Supreme Court sentences Bolsonaro's son over US lobbying 17/06/2026 Americas After a long wait, JR's Pont Neuf installation opens to the public 17/06/2026 France Paris's BHV ends short but controversial partnership with Shein 17/06/2026 France DR Congo Ebola outbreak could become worst in history as thousands not being traced 17/06/2026 Africa US signals to return of sanctions on Russia as G7 unites around Ukraine 17/06/2026 Europe Thousands flock back to south Lebanon despite Israeli strikes amid US-Iran deal 17/06/2026 Middle East Paris's largest outside swimming pool opens early ahead of massive heatwave 17/06/2026 France UN chief visits Haiti ahead of new gang suppression force deployment 17/06/2026 Americas"
